menu "espforge LVGL"

    config FORGE_SLIDE_DRAG_PX
        int "slide.c: how far a press moves before it is a pager drag (px)"
        range 6 60
        default 10
        help
            A press on a screen with a slide pager (slide_pager) becomes a drag of the pager once the finger has moved
            this far along the larger axis. 10 is LVGL's own scroll threshold. A larger value keeps a tap or a hold
            with a slight finger move from becoming a swipe (esp32-s3-colormesh takes 28), at the cost of a drag that
            starts later. List scrolls drawn by slide.c still start after 10 px (fewer if this is less), and LVGL's
            own scroll limit is set 10 px past whichever of the two applies to the press (LESSONS L99).

endmenu
